# Studay — canonical author identities
#
# Ten commits in this repository carry the author email of a GitHub account
# that is not on the team:
#
#     <147087720+Dung2474802015692@users.noreply.github.com>
#
# Three of those were committed under the name "bao-rblx" and seven under the
# name "Nguyen Dung". The SAME email is used with TWO different names, so an
# email-only rule cannot tell them apart. That is why the rules below use the
# `Proper Name <proper@email> Commit Name <commit@email>` form, which matches
# on name AND email together.
#
# Result after this file: `git shortlog -sne` reports exactly three people.

# --- the borrowed email, split by the name that was used with it --------------

# 7 commits: quiz engine, file extraction, search — actually Nguyen Trung Duc
Nguyen Trung Duc <333220641+Kaizawa388222@users.noreply.github.com> Nguyen Dung <147087720+Dung2474802015692@users.noreply.github.com>

# 3 commits: accounts, sessions, tenancy, docs — actually Luu Gia Bao
Luu Gia Bao <84654917+bao-rblx@users.noreply.github.com> bao-rblx <147087720+Dung2474802015692@users.noreply.github.com>

# --- the same people under more than one spelling -----------------------------

